597 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (At this stage, initial data cleaning was performed. Using Column Filter, service and text variables that do not contain useful information for predicting the severity of accidents \(text descriptions, IDs, address fields, etc.\) were removed, and in the Mission Value knife, missing values in weather variables \(temperature, wind speed, humidity, pressure, visibility, precipitation, etc.\) were replaced with the median for the column.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
598 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In this part, the main feature transformations were performed. Using Rule Engine, the Weather_Group variable was created, which aggregates detailed text descriptions of the weather into several understandable categories \(CLEAR, CLOUDY, RAIN, SNOW, FOG, etc.\). At the same time, the target variable Severity_bin was formed: this indicator reflects not the medical consequences of road accidents, which are absent in the dataset, but is determined by the degree of their impact on road traffic, where values 3-4 are classified as serious accidents.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
599 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The final stage of data preparation involves transforming the Start_Time variable, converting it to datetime format, and extracting the hour, day of the week, and month. Additionally, Rush_Hour and Weekend flags are generated to reflect the main time patterns of traffic accidents.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
