/E (The initial Weather_Condition change contained a large number of rare heterogeneous text values, which complicated modeling and interpretation. Using the Rule Engine node, these records were aggregated into several generalized categories: CLEAR, CLOUDY, RAIN, SNOW, FOG, and OTHER. This grouping reduces the number of unique factor levels, eliminates random, infrequent values, and converts weather information into a more consistent and analytically useful format. As a result, the Weather_Group variable became compact, stable, and fully suitable for use in modeling traffic accident severity classifications.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
