/E (The Severity variable in the source dataset, represented by four levels, was converted into a binary indicator Severity_bin using the Rule Engine node. Values 3 and 4 are designated as serious accidents, while values 1 and 2 refer to non-serious cases. It is important to emphasize that the Severity variable in this dataset reflects not the medical consequences of an accident, but the degree of its impact on traffic. This logic allows the task to be formulated as a clear binary classification and ensures the consistency of subsequent forecasting models.)
/Pg 20 0 R
