/E (Before running Random Forest models, we perform a separate feature cleaning step using the Column Filter node. At this stage, variables that should not be included in the model are removed from the data: the target variable Severity, as well as time and text fields \(Start_Time, Weather_Timestamp, Weather_Condition\). All other spatial, weather, and infrastructure variables remain as potential predictors. This step ensures that the model is trained correctly: it receives only allowed predictors, does not contain explicit information about the target, and maintains the consistency of the input feature set for all three Random Forest configurations \(balanced, simple, reduced\). This also ensures the correctness of further comparison of models with each other.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [1]
>>
