716 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ($#splits\(level 0\)$ + $#splits\(level 1\)$ + $#splits\(level 2\)$ sums up how many times the tree splits the data at the key first levels. This does not affect the forecast itself, but adds an indicator of model complexity: the more splits, the more intensively the model searches for patterns. Each branch adds its own column so that the complexity of the three versions of Random Forest can be compared with each other. All formulas are the same, only the column names differ for ease of analysis.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [6]
>>
