/E (The H2O Gradient Boosting Machine Learner model builds an ensemble of weak decision trees, where each subsequent tree corrects the errors of the previous ones. Severity_bin is used as the target variable. The model includes all selected weather, time, geographic, and infrastructure features. Key hyperparameters, such as tree depth, learning rate, and number of models, determine the complexity and ability of the model to generalize patterns. GBM is robust to nonlinearities and interactions between features, making it effective for predicting the severity of traffic accidents.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [1]
>>
