/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The MLP was first tested on the full U.S. dataset, but its performance was very poor due to the high geographic and infrastructural heterogeneity across states. Neural networks are sensitive to such variability, and a single national model could not learn consistent patterns. Since the tree-based models had already shown State to be one of the strongest predictors of severity, we shifted to a state-specific MLP approach, training a separate model for each state. This provides more homogeneous data for learning, improves model performance, and allows us to examine how accident severity behaves across different regions.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
