938 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Both models overwhelmingly agree that State is the strongest predictor of accident severity. Both highlight Distance, Wind Direction, and multiple weather-related variables as critical determinants. XGBoost spreads importance more granularly across continuous variables and captures subtle nonlinear interactions. Random Forest concentrates importance on features that consistently produce stable splits across the ensemble. The consistency across models strongly reinforces the conclusion that accident severity is shaped by geographic conditions, road infrastructure, and regional weather patterns. This convergence across two distinct algorithms provides robust evidence supporting the state-level heterogeneity highlighted earlier and strengthens the managerial implications presented later in the report.)
/Pg 68 0 R
/K [8]
>>
