/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Our analysis reveals a consistent and compelling message across all models: accident severity in the United States is predominantly shaped by geographic and infrastructural differences across states, rather than by isolated crash-level characteristics alone. This finding has direct implications for policy-makers, transportation authorities, emergency services, and insurance companies seeking to allocate resources effectively and design targeted interventions.)
/Pg 72 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
